* commit 34f36d99a7fca2de00227eea4aef4774820b8940
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Tue May 5 15:27:49 2026 -0700
| 
|     docs: alsoletter={'} + add eexists / ex_intro / all to keywords
|     
|     Three related listing fixes triggered by review of section 2.5.4:
|     
|     1. The keyword [iter] was being highlighted *inside* the identifiers
|        [iter'] and [iter'_equiv] -- listings' default letter set is
|        [A-Za-z], so [iter'] tokenizes as the three pieces [iter] + ['] +
|        [_equiv], and the [iter] keyword matched the prefix.  This is
|        the same kind of word-boundary failure we hit earlier with [exists]
|        inside [exists_maximizer_42], but with [']-as-separator instead
|        of [_]-as-separator.
|     
|        Fix: add [alsoletter={'}] to the [\lstdefinelanguage{Coq}{...}]
|        block.  This tells listings to treat ['] as a letter for the
|        purposes of identifier tokenization, which matches Coq's actual
|        identifier grammar (Coq identifiers are
|        [[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_']*]).  After the fix, [iter'] is one
|        token and [iter] no longer matches its prefix.
|     
|     2. Added [eexists] to [morekeywords].  [eexists] is the existential-
|        introduction tactic ([e]-variant of [exists] -- same convention
|        as [eapply], [eauto]) that postpones witness instantiation by
|        creating a fresh existential variable.  Used in
|        [ack'_reification_helper]'s proof.
|     
|     3. Added [ex_intro] to [morekeywords].  [ex_intro] is the
|        constructor of Coq's [ex] (existential proposition); used here
|        in pattern-matching on a previously-built [exists] proof to
|        extract the witness.  Same family as [Some] / [None] / [cons] /
|        [nil] / [existT] which were already keywords.
|     
|     4. Added [all] to [morekeywords].  [all] is the all-subgoals
|        selector in Coq's proof-script syntax: [all: tac.] applies
|        [tac] to every currently-open subgoal.  It is part of the
|        selector family ([1: tac.], [2: tac.], [1-3: tac.],
|        [[name]: tac.]) and is unmistakably syntactic.
|     
|     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
| 
