* commit e8b4383429589ae600d438a5524c650a209947b0
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Mon May 4 16:15:53 2026 -0700
| 
|     docs: render [<-], [/\], [\/] as math glyphs in code listings
|     
|     Three more literate rules joining the existing arrow / inequality
|     substitutions:
|     
|       [<-]  -> [\leftarrow]   (Coq's reverse-rewrite tactic argument,
|                                e.g. [rewrite <- (witness_grow_eval ...)])
|       [/\]  -> [\land]        (logical AND in Coq propositions)
|       [\/] -> [\lor]         (logical OR in Coq propositions)
|     
|     None of these tokens can appear inside a Coq identifier ([_] is the
|     only non-alphanumeric identifier character), so the literate
|     substitution is unambiguous in a way that [exists]/[forall] were
|     not.
|     
|     The [\] in the patterns is the [listings]/[TeX] escape for a single
|     backslash, so [{/\}] matches the two-character source token [/\]
|     (slash + backslash) and [{\/}] matches [\/] (backslash + slash).
|     
|     The longer [<->]-pattern is moved to the top of the [literate]
|     block so it has match priority over the new [<-] (a 3-char prefix
|     of [<->] would otherwise eat the [<-] before [<->] gets a chance).
|     
|     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
