* commit 4b7ded6a92eda189f47af7eb3a029d9bd46b86cd
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Mon May 4 14:49:50 2026 -0700
| 
|     docs: render \llbracket / \rrbracket distinctively at every zoom
|     
|     Two earlier attempts misbehaved:
|     
|       1. The original fallback [\llbracket = [\!\![] uses [\!] (negative
|          thin space, $-3$mu) twice, overlapping the two [[] glyphs by
|          enough that at small zoom they read as a single bold bracket.
|     
|       2. Adding [\usepackage{stmaryrd}] loads the package, but its
|          [stmary10] font is not bundled with [lualatex]'s default
|          [luaotfload] cache, so every [\llbracket] / [\rrbracket]
|          rendered as a missing-character box and dropped from the output
|          entirely.
|     
|     This change drops the [stmaryrd] dependency and tightens the manual
|     fallback: [\mathopen{[\mkern-2.5mu[}] (and the [\mathclose] dual).
|     The [-2.5mu] kern is just enough overlap to make the pair read as a
|     single double-bracket symbol, but loose enough that the two [[]
|     glyphs stay visibly distinct at every reasonable zoom level.  The
|     [\mathopen]/[\mathclose] wrappers also restore correct math-mode
|     spacing around the symbol (otherwise [\llbracket A \rrbracket]
|     would be typeset with relation-spacing instead of bracket-spacing).
|     
|     Now [tpNat], [tpArr A B], etc. inside [[..]] render unambiguously
|     as double-bracket interpretation brackets at every zoom level.
