|     docs: add contender_6.tex tutorial
|     
|     A self-contained LaTeX tutorial walk-through of [contender_6], suitable
|     both as a companion piece to the [submit-c6-prep] branch's modifications
|     to [Contender.v] and as a standalone introduction to the construction.
|     
|     Compiles to a roughly 18-page PDF with [lualatex] (or [pdflatex] +
|     [stmaryrd]).  The article covers, in tutorial form:
|     
|       - the [name-the-biggest-number] contest setting and the
|         [don't-be-lazy] rule;
|     
|       - Brouwer ordinal notations and why fundamental-sequence-as-data
|         turns ordinal recursion into ordinary structural recursion;
|     
|       - the fast-growing hierarchy and its closure properties up through
|         [BigGrow := f_{epsilon_0}];
|     
|       - the new object language [L_Grow] (System T plus a fresh
|         [tGrow] primitive) and its denotational semantics, including the
|         polymorphic [pack] type and the [eval] extractor;
|     
|       - the embedding [embed_term : Contender.term -> term] and a
|         Tait-style logical relation that proves it preserves evaluation
|         *without* function extensionality;
|     
|       - the witness term [tGrow (S (embed t_star))] at depth 44, where
|         [t_star] is the existential maximiser of [contender_5];
|     
|       - the chain of inequalities
|     
|           contender_5 < BigGrow (S contender_5) <= contender_6.
|     
|     Each step quotes the corresponding Coq fragment verbatim from the
|     inlined [Contender.v].  Bibliographical pointers to Aaronson's
|     original essay, Tait's logical-relation paper, and the
|     Schwichtenberg-Wainer textbook are included.
|     
|     The PDF artefact is *not* checked in; the [.tex] source is the
|     canonical version.
