| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Thu Apr 30 22:14:15 2026 -0700
| 
|     Approach M: complete the GrowEmbed sandbox (axiom-free, clean defn)
|     
|     Picks up where commit 8cbedfe left off (WIP: start Approach M GrowEmbed
|     sandbox, blocked in [embed_interp_related] tVar case).
|     
|     ** What landed **
|     
|     * sandbox/GrowEmbed.v now compiles in ~1.5 s, [coqchk] accepts the
|       module, and Print Assumptions reports closed global contexts for the
|       two end-state theorems exposed at file top level:
|     
|         Definition contender_grow_6 : nat := BigGrowEmbed.contender_grow_6.
|         Theorem  BigGrow_lower_bound :
|           Brouwer.BigGrow (S Contender.contender_5) <= contender_grow_6.
|         Theorem  contender_5_lt_contender_grow_6 :
|           Contender.contender_5 < contender_grow_6.
|     
|     * contender_grow_6 = largest_Grow_nat_of_depth 44 -- definitionally
|       clean.  scripts/check_cleanliness.py confirms both
|       [sandbox.GrowEmbed.contender_grow_6] and the inner
|       [sandbox.GrowEmbed.BigGrowEmbed.contender_grow_6] PASS the
|       don't-be-lazy check (no banned-engine identifiers in the body).
|     
|     * The proof uses a Tait-style logical relation
|       [RelVal : type -> interp_type tp -> interp_type tp -> Prop] that
|       collapses to plain equality at [tpNat], so [embed_eval] goes through
|       with no functional-extensionality dependency.
|     
|     ** Engineering issues fixed **
|     
|     The previous agent got stuck (per the WIP commit message and reviews/
|     analysis) on five specific issues; each is now resolved and documented
|     inline in IDEAS.md "Approach M -- Status (2026-05-01): COMPLETE".
|     
|     1. [destruct EXPR eqn:E1] does not substitute the scrutinee inside a
|        surrounding [match] in this Coq version.  Subsequent [rewrite E1]
|        then fails.  Worked around by proving self-contained reduction
|        lemmas (Contender_interp_term_tVar_Some, etc.) outside the main
|        induction and rewriting via those.
|     
|     2. Contender.eval / Contender.largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth are
|        kept Opaque at file scope (so the kernel never tries to enumerate
|        the depth-42 search).  embed_eval and contender_5_ge_1 need to
|        peek inside; wrapped them in [Local Transparent ... Local Opaque]
|        bracket.
|     
|     3. Coq's [existT (fun tp => ...)] vs. [existT name] eta forms don't
|        auto-convert under [rewrite].  Sidestepped by [replace]-ing at the
|        pack level rather than the existT level.
|     
|     4. [have ... { ... }] is an SSReflect tactic, not standard Coq.
|        Replaced with [assert ... by ...].
|     
|     5. [Theorem name : type := body.] is a syntax error in this Coq.
|        The end-of-file alias theorems are now [Definition]s.
|     
|     ** Other changes **
|     
|     * scripts/check_cleanliness.py: drop the generic [largest_of_depth]
|       from BANNED -- fresh-engine sandboxes (like L_Grow) define their
|       own [largest_of_depth] and a substring match would falsely flag
|       them.  The more specific [largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth] is
|       retained.  Also added the new GrowEmbed contenders to the default
|       CANDIDATES list.
|     
|     * scripts/audit_assumptions.py: added [contender_grow_6] and
|       [BigGrow_lower_bound] to EXTRAS so they appear in the default
|       audit table.
|     
|     * AGENTS.md / IDEAS.md: removed all WIP markers around Approach M,
|       added the COMPLETE status block recording the five engineering
|       issues for future relay agents.
|     
|     ** Status of the audit table **
|     
|     23 theorems closed under the global context (now including
|     [sandbox.GrowEmbed.contender_5_lt_contender_grow_6]); 3 still depend
|     on functional_extensionality_dep (the ReflectTower / ReflectRTower
|     variants kept as historical reference).
|     
|     ** Cleanliness summary **
|     
|     5 candidates clean, 8 LAZY.  The 5 clean ones:
|     - sandbox.Brouwer.BigGrow
|     - sandbox.BrouwerHigh.BigGrow_e_omega
|     - sandbox.BrouwerHigh.BigGrow_pseudo_Gamma_0
|     - sandbox.GrowEmbed.contender_grow_6  <-- new
|     - sandbox.GrowEmbed.BigGrowEmbed.contender_grow_6  <-- new
|     
|     This is the first sandbox candidate that combines (a) a fresh-engine
|     clean definition and (b) a strict-inequality proof against
|     contender_5, without using contender_5's machinery in the definition
|     or any axioms beyond Coq's logic.
