| |     
| |     * `_CoqProject`: standard Coq project marker, just `-Q . ""`.
| |       Lets coq-lsp and coqdep work without per-invocation flags.
| |     
| |     * `scripts/build.py` (~190 lines).  Discovers .v files at the repo
| |       root and in sandbox/, parses Require lines to derive a dependency
| |       graph, topologically sorts, rebuilds anything whose .vo is older
| |       than its .v or any dependency's .vo, and reports per-file compile
| |       times.  Flags: --clean, --force, --check (coqchk after each
| |       build), --all (include archival files), --timeout, plus a single
| |       positional argument to build one file and its prerequisites.
| |       Skips Graveyard.v / Shenannigans.v / System_F.v by default
| |       because they are archival, paradox-using, or don't compile on
| |       Rocq 9.0.1.
| |     
| |     * `scripts/audit_assumptions.py` (~230 lines).  Auto-discovers
| |       theorems whose names match `contender_*_lt_*` across the active
| |       sandbox, plus a small fixed EXTRAS list (Contender.contender_5,
| |       Brouwer.BigGrow, BrouwerHigh.pseudo_Gamma_0, etc.), generates a
| |       temporary .v file at the repo root running `Print Assumptions T`
| |       on each, parses coqc output, and writes a Markdown table reporting
| |       status (OK / AXIOMS / UNKNOWN) and any axiom dependencies.
| |       --md / --json options for persisting the report.  Exit code is 1
| |       when any theorem still depends on axioms.
| |     
| |     * `scripts/README.md`: usage notes, including the explicit non-goals
| |       (no replacement of in-editor proof tooling; no cleanliness lint;
| |       no CI; no cross-version testing) and where to extend each script.
| |     
| |     Tested end-to-end on the current ideas-branch state.  build.py
| |     rebuilds the 15 active .v files in ~13 s on this machine and
| |     correctly skips up-to-date files in 0 s.  audit_assumptions.py
| |     discovers 17 strict-inequality theorems plus 6 extras, correctly
| |     flags the three FunExt-tainted reflection-tower theorems, and
| |     reports the rest as closed under the global context.
| |     
| |     Engineering details:
| |     
| |     * Module discovery in audit_assumptions.py strips Coq comments via
| |       a small balanced-paren walker before applying its regex; nested
| |       (* (* *) *) comments are handled.  Section / Module Type / Module
| |       Import are deliberately not tracked as module openers (they
| |       don't add to qualified names in our codebase).
| |     
| |     * All output is ASCII-only -- Windows cp1252 consoles can't print
| |       ✅ / ⚠️ / ❓ so the reports use **OK** / **AXIOMS** / **UNKNOWN**
| |       bold-text instead.
| |     
| |     * Both scripts anchor on their own location via Path(__file__).resolve(),
| |       so they can be invoked from any working directory.
| | 
